    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and the suite is green. Done.\n\nI implemented the customerCode de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- `populateDerivedFields` now calls a new `deriveUniqueCustomerCode(owner)` instead of setting the raw derived code.\n- `deriveUniqueCustomerCode` computes the base code via `identityKeyResolver.deriveCustomerCode(owner)`, then checks it against all existing owners' `customerCode`s. On collision it appends `-<n>`, incrementing from `2` upward until the whole code is unique, and returns that value.\n\nThis runs before the owner is saved (so it compares only against pre-existing owners) and keeps the base code untouched when there's no collision, guaranteeing distinct owners get distinct customer codes. The build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).",
